  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contracting in Illinois is concentrated and reduced in FY2027 to date. The state shows total obligations of $245M across 8,731 awards, with an average award size of $28.1K and obligations down 98.0% year over year. Historical fiscal-year totals show much larger rounds of spending: FY22 totaled $13.6B, FY23 totaled $13B, FY24 totaled $13.4B, FY25 totaled $12.4B, and FY26 totaled $12B. Top industries in FY2027 to date include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $81.1M and Analytical Laboratory Instrument Manufacturing at $40.2M. Top vendors include UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC at $81.1M and ABBOTT LABORATORIES INC. at $25.9M. Top buying agencies in FY2027 to date include the Department of Veterans Affairs at $139M and the Department of Energy at $81.1M. All figures are contract obligations; FY2027 totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have federal contract obligations in Illinois changed year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 98.0% year over year in FY2027 to date compared with prior full fiscal years. Illinois recorded $245M in obligations for FY2027 to date, after totals of $13.6B in FY22, $13B in FY23, $13.4B in FY24, $12.4B in FY25, and $12B in FY26. The average award size in FY2027 to date is $28.1K across 8,731 awards. The FY2027 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors lead federal contracting in Illinois in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $139M and the Department of Energy obligated $81.1M in FY2027 to date. UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC received $81.1M and ABBOTT LABORATORIES INC. received $25.9M in FY2027 to date. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the top industry at $81.1M and Analytical Laboratory Instrument Manufacturing is second at $40.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
